==Finnish==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|fi|fin-fin-pro|*eci}}, from {{inh|fi|fiu-pro|*ede}}; a cognate of Hungarian {{term|lang=hu|elő}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|lang=fi|[ˈe̞si]}}
* {{rhymes|esi|lang=fi}}
* {{hyphenation|e|si|lang=fi}}

===Prefix===
{{fi-pref}}

# [[pre-]], [[fore-]].

====Inflection====
{{fi-decl-pron|type=käsi|1s=[[esi-]]|5s=[[edessä]]|6s=[[edestä]]|7s=[[eteen]]|8s=[[edellä]]|9s=[[edeltä]]|10s=[[edelle]]|13s=[[etenkin]]<br/>[[etenkään]]|7p=[[esiin]]|8p=[[esillä]]|9p=[[esiltä]]|10p=[[esille]]|a4s=([[edes]])|a10s=[[editse]]}}
The cases of {{term|esi-|lang=fi}} serve in Finnish only as adverbs. The instructive singular is always used with the enclitic particle {{term|lang=fi|-kin}} or {{term|lang=fi|-kään}}.
Declension scheme is the same as type 27 ([[Appendix:Finnish nominal inflection/käsi|käsi]]), except of some missing, not used forms; and the two extra instructive singular forms [[etenkin]] and [[etenkään]].

====Antonyms====
* {{sense|pre-, fore-}} [[jälki-]]

